Layer1a — CosmaChain Smart Contracts

Layer1a‑Smart‑Contracts is the programmable on‑chain engine of the CosmaTech ecosystem. It defines identity‑bound transactions, benefits agreements, revenue splits, booking logic, economic scoring, and domain‑specific contracts for CosmaCare, CosmaStar, CosmaGigs, FilmCore, CaddiePro, and CosmaSocial. All logic executes through a Rust‑based VM and dispatcher.

2. Purpose
Layer1a provides the execution logic for all CosmaTech protocols and apps.
It is responsible for:

Defining domain‑specific smart contracts

Executing contract code through a Rust‑based VM

Managing contract state, events, and identity‑bound transactions

Powering benefits, revenue splits, settlements, and service logic

Anchoring all Layer‑2 protocol outputs to Layer‑1

Providing a unified contract engine for all Layer‑4 apps

This layer is the heart of CosmaTech’s programmable benefits engine.

3. Functions
Core Engine Functions
Contract VM execution

Contract dispatching

ABI parsing

Contract state management

Event emission

Identity‑bound transaction enforcement

Domain Contract Functions
Benefits agreements

Revenue splits

Booking logic (CosmaCare)

Service definitions (CosmaStar, CosmaGigs, FilmCore, CaddiePro)

Settlement logic

Social graph interactions (CosmaSocial)

Protocol Functions
S3E2C3 behavioral scoring

ESEC economic scoring

Identity‑bound transactions

Taxable event detection

Treasury routing

Token mint/burn logic (via Layer‑2 tokens)

